email: Required for each manager entry when UID is disabled. Must be a valid email format; an invalid value returns an HTTP 400 error. key: Mindtickle relationship shortkey for the Manager attribute. Note: To clear a manager assignment, set the identifier value to NONE (uppercase). See the Additional info section for an example. |

Request example

The identifier you provide depends on whether UID is enabled for your Mindtickle instance.

When UID is enabled — identify the user and each manager by username:

```json
{
  "name": "Alex Fry",
  "username": "alex.fry@mindtickle.com",
  "id": "123456abcd",
  "timezone": "America/Costa_Rica",
  "profile": {
    "dp": "abc",
    "lang": "Italian"
  },
  "groupIds": [
    "123456789009876"
  ],
  "seriesEntities": [
    {
      "seriesId": "12345678909871",
      "entities": [
        "123454156256787698"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "managers": [
    {
      "username": "james.smith@mindtickle.com",
      "key": "a_0"
    }
  ]
}
```

When UID is disabled — identify the user and each manager by email. The username field is not used and can be omitted:

```json
{
  "name": "Alex Fry",
  "email": "alex.fry@mindtickle.com",
  "id": "123456abcd",
  "timezone": "America/Costa_Rica",
  "profile": {
    "dp": "abc",
    "lang": "Italian"
  },
  "groupIds": [
    "123456789009876"
  ],
  "seriesEntities": [
    {
      "seriesId": "12345678909871",
      "entities": [
        "123454156256787698"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "managers": [
    {
      "email": "james.smith@mindtickle.com",
      "key": "a_0"
    }
  ]
}
```

Response fields

| Name | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| requestId | string | null |
| responseCode | string | Special response codes from the server. |
| responseType | string | Type of response from the server. |
