Help & Support > Help Center Home > Mindtickle APIs > Copilot APIs > Chat API > Response:
Response parameters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | string | A unique identifier for the chat session. |
| created | int | The timestamp when the chat session was created. |
| username | string | The username of the Mindtickle user who initiated the chat. |
| output | object | Contains the assistant's response and metadata. The object includes:output.index (int): Incremental chunk index (starts at 0).output.response(array): An array of assistant's responses. Each response contains:response.role (string): The role of the responder (assistant).response.content(array): The actual response text.content.type (string): The type of content (currently "text").content.text (string): The assistant's response text.content.annotations(array): Links to reference content used to generate the response.annotations.type (string): Type of annotation (currently "link").annotations.url (string): The URL of the annotated content.annotations.title (string): The title of the annotated content.tags (array): Tags associated with the generated response.usage (object): Reserved for future token usage information. Left blank intentionally currently. |
| status | string | Assistant response status (in_progress, completed, failed); final chunk status is completed. |
| error | object | Includes error details if a chunk response has a failedstatus:error.code (string): HTTP code of the error received from the Copilot servererror.message (string): Error message in natural language received from the copilot server |

Response example

```json

{
  "id": "chatcmpl-123",
  "created": 1700000000,
  "username": "dummy-user",
  "output": {
    "index": 0,
    "response": [
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "output_text",
            "text": "Sample response text.",
            "annotations": [
              {
