Help & Support > Help Center Home > Mindtickle APIs > Copilot APIs > Chat API > Streaming event details:
The Chat API supports server-sent events (SSE) for real-time streaming responses:

- Initial chunk : The assistant starts responding incrementally.
- Final chunk : The full response is completed.
- Error chunk : If an error occurs, the response will indicate a failed status with error details.

Streaming response examples

A. Initial chunk

```json

{
  "id": "dummy-query-1743673664",
  "created": 1743673664179,
  "username": "dummy-user",
  "output": {
    "index": 0,
    "tags": ["ai-generated"],
    "response": [
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is dummy streaming message 1 of 10"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "status": "in_progress"
}
```

B. Final chunk

```json

{
  "id": "dummy-query-1743673664",
  "created": 1743673669192,
  "username": "dummy-user",
  "output": {
    "index": 11,
    "tags": ["ai-generated"],
    "response": [
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "All 10 streaming messages completed."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "status": "completed"
}
```

C. Error chunk

```json

{
  "id": "dummy-query-1743673664",
  "created": 0,
  "username": "dummy-user",
  "output": null,
  "error": {
    "code": "400",
    "message": "Bad Request - Missing required parameter - input.role."
  },
  "status": "failed"
}
```

